── Viseme model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

packages/viseme uses `wav2arkit`, a single ONNX graph exported by combining two upstream
models. It is a derivative work of both, and is redistributed under the same terms.

  facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h                          Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h
  Used as the audio encoder.

  3DAIGC/LAM_audio2exp  (aigc3d/LAM_Audio2Expression)  Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/3DAIGC/LAM_audio2exp
  Used as the expression decoder, producing 52 ARKit blendshapes.

Modification: the two models were combined and exported to a single ONNX graph for CPU
inference. No weights were retrained or fine-tuned.

The model weights are not committed to this repository; see packages/viseme/README.md for
how to obtain them.


── Bundled face pack (assets/emma) ─────────────────────────────────────────────

The portrait and its mouth-shape library are synthetic. No real person is depicted.

  Base portrait          generated with Z-Image Turbo (Tongyi-MAI / Alibaba)
                         https://huggingface.co/Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo
                         Model released under Apache License 2.0.

  Mouth and eye shapes   generated with Qwen-Image-Edit (Alibaba)
                         Model released under Apache License 2.0.

  Idle video clips       generated with Google Veo 3.1 via the Gemini API.
                         Google does not claim ownership of generated output and permits
                         commercial use and redistribution. Output may carry an invisible
                         SynthID provenance watermark; the clips here were letterboxed-
                         cropped and re-encoded, which was not done to affect it.

Generation parameters for every asset are recorded in docs/face-packs.md so the pack can be
rebuilt or replaced.


── Voices ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

No voice model or voice account is bundled. The TTS adapters in packages/server/src/tts.js
call software or services you supply:

  macOS `say`, espeak-ng     local, no account
  Fish Audio, OpenAI TTS     your own account; commercial rights and any voice-cloning
                             consent are governed by your agreement with that provider

Cloning a voice requires the consent of the person whose voice it is. This project bundles
no cloned voice and takes no position on yours.
